# What `docker build` leaves out of the app image.
# Settings stay on the server: .env holds the secret key and payment keys, and is passed in at run time
# (env_file in docker-compose.yml). Copied into the image it would also be unreadable by the app's user
# once .env is locked to root (chmod 600), which stops the app from starting.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Data, history and local clutter
instance/
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-*
.git
.github
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
